   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Chroma1-HD text to image (8.9B, Apache 2.0), with a real CFG so the negative prompt works. 26 steps, 1024x1024 by default. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: Chroma likes long, natural sentences more than keyword lists.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid, also in sentences.\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024 (16:9 = 1360x768). Leave \"multiple\" at 16.\n   - **Steps** (26) and **CFG** (3.5): the template's values.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026, so the first Run gives the README picture. Type a new number (or set \"control after generate\" to randomize) for a new picture; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Flow shift stays at 1.\n3. **Prompt**: nothing to change. T5 padding 0 / 0 is the template value (the template note says min_padding 1 is the official one; both work).\n4. **Sampling**: euler / beta, from the template.\n5. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/Chroma/`.\n\n**What to expect:** about 46-47 s per 1024x1024 picture at 26 steps on the lab's 24 GB card (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell), first run included; 16:9 (1360x768) took 47 s. In a 10 GiB VRAM budget the same pictures took 49-50 s and came out byte-identical.\n\n**Text in the picture** is hit or miss: the default seed wrote \"CHROMA 1 -HD\", seed 777 wrote \"CHROMA-HI\". Try a few seeds.\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 2026-11-24. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
