   "title": "Downloads + requirements",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Downloads + requirements\n\nClick the file name to download it. Put it in the folder shown (inside `ComfyUI/models/`).\n\n| Folder | File (click = download) | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `diffusion_models/` | [Chroma1-HD-fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Chroma1-HD_repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/Chroma1-HD-fp8mixed.safetensors) | 9.19 GB |\n| `text_encoders/` | [t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors) | 5.16 GB |\n| `vae/` | [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Lumina_Image_2.0_Repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors) | 0.34 GB |\n\nIf you already run Flux.1, you have the T5 and the VAE. Full-precision model (17.8 GB, not tested here): `Chroma1-HD.safetensors` in the same Comfy-Org repo.\n\n**VRAM:** ComfyUI uses what it is given: 16.4 GiB on a free 24 GB card. A second ComfyUI limited to a 10 GiB budget (`--reserve-vram`) peaked at 10.1 GiB (11.0 GiB whole GPU), took 49-50 s (47 s without a limit) and gave byte-identical pictures. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n\n**Run on ComfyUI 0.45.3** (older versions were not tested). **No custom nodes.**\n\nLicence: Chroma1-HD is Apache 2.0.\n"
   ]
  }
